<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><ncx xmlns="http://www.daisy.org/z3986/2005/ncx/" version="2005-1" xml:lang="en"><head><meta name="dtb:uid" content="urn:uuid:20b6d6a2-7e0a-4f03-a80c-c83cbb787030"/><meta name="dtb:depth" content="2"/><meta name="dtb:totalPageCount" content="0"/><meta name="dtb:maxPageNumber" content="0"/></head><docTitle><text>The sovereign debt chain</text></docTitle><navMap><navPoint id="nav-1" playOrder="1"><navLabel><text>Read the contracts, dates and scope</text></navLabel><content src="text/method.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-2" playOrder="2"><navLabel><text>Introduction: One bond, several lives</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch001.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-3" playOrder="3"><navLabel><text>1. The first buyer</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml"/><navPoint id="nav-4" playOrder="4"><navLabel><text>Fresh borrowing also pays yesterday’s creditors</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#fresh-borrowing-also-pays-yesterdays-creditors"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-5" playOrder="5"><navLabel><text>At 10:50 a.m., prices come before names</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#at-1050-am-prices-come-before-names"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-6" playOrder="6"><navLabel><text>The coupon stays still while the price falls</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#the-coupon-stays-still-while-the-price-falls"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-7" playOrder="7"><navLabel><text>The following day, the issue gets bigger</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#the-following-day-the-issue-gets-bigger"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-8" playOrder="8"><navLabel><text>When the promise becomes a payment</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#when-the-promise-becomes-a-payment"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-9" playOrder="9"><navLabel><text>In the United States, dealers bid heavily and receive little</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#in-the-united-states-dealers-bid-heavily-and-receive-little"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-10" playOrder="10"><navLabel><text>An auction establishes a price and leaves questions open</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#an-auction-establishes-a-price-and-leaves-questions-open"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-11" playOrder="11"><navLabel><text>How far can the creditor actually be identified?</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#how-far-can-the-creditor-actually-be-identified"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-12" playOrder="12"><navLabel><text>Sources and reading notes</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#sources-and-reading-notes"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-13" playOrder="13"><navLabel><text>2. The price of a dealer’s balance sheet</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml"/><navPoint id="nav-14" playOrder="14"><navLabel><text>The leaders change once the bonds start trading</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#the-leaders-change-once-the-bonds-start-trading"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-15" playOrder="15"><navLabel><text>Buying time between two investors</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#buying-time-between-two-investors"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-16" playOrder="16"><navLabel><text>The bond leaves; the financing remains</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#the-bond-leaves-the-financing-remains"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-17" playOrder="17"><navLabel><text>Several limits, several decision-makers</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#several-limits-several-decision-makers"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-18" playOrder="18"><navLabel><text>Washington creates regulatory room</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#washington-creates-regulatory-room"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-19" playOrder="19"><navLabel><text>Eight banks, two positive responses</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#eight-banks-two-positive-responses"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-20" playOrder="20"><navLabel><text>The client expecting another loan</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#the-client-expecting-another-loan"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-21" playOrder="21"><navLabel><text>More circulation from the same balance sheets</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#more-circulation-from-the-same-balance-sheets"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-22" playOrder="22"><navLabel><text>The cost reaches the state through the price</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#the-cost-reaches-the-state-through-the-price"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-23" playOrder="23"><navLabel><text>Sources and reading notes</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#sources-and-reading-notes"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-24" playOrder="24"><navLabel><text>3. The buyers who borrow</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml"/><navPoint id="nav-25" playOrder="25"><navLabel><text>Using futures to adjust interest-rate exposure</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#using-futures-to-adjust-interest-rate-exposure"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-26" playOrder="26"><navLabel><text>A price difference that must survive until exit</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#a-price-difference-that-must-survive-until-exit"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-27" playOrder="27"><navLabel><text>A hundred million in bonds, three million in capital</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#a-hundred-million-in-bonds-three-million-in-capital"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-28" playOrder="28"><navLabel><text>Funding can absorb the return</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#funding-can-absorb-the-return"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-29" playOrder="29"><navLabel><text>Margin calls create an immediate cash requirement</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#margin-calls-create-an-immediate-cash-requirement"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-30" playOrder="30"><navLabel><text>The strategies behind the totals</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#the-strategies-behind-the-totals"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-31" playOrder="31"><navLabel><text>April 2025: two trades, different paths</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#april-2025-two-trades-different-paths"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-32" playOrder="32"><navLabel><text>Selling before the lender says stop</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#selling-before-the-lender-says-stop"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-33" playOrder="33"><navLabel><text>A conditional creditor</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#a-conditional-creditor"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-34" playOrder="34"><navLabel><text>Sources and reading notes</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#sources-and-reading-notes"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-35" playOrder="35"><navLabel><text>4. The collateral chain</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml"/><navPoint id="nav-36" playOrder="36"><navLabel><text>The cash behind the loan</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#the-cash-behind-the-loan"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-37" playOrder="37"><navLabel><text>A $100 million portfolio supports two loans</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#a-100-million-portfolio-supports-two-loans"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-38" playOrder="38"><navLabel><text>Ownership moves; the exposure remains</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#ownership-moves-the-exposure-remains"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-39" playOrder="39"><navLabel><text>The dealer’s calendar</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#the-dealers-calendar"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-40" playOrder="40"><navLabel><text>Zero haircuts and negotiated protection</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#zero-haircuts-and-negotiated-protection"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-41" playOrder="41"><navLabel><text>Existing collateral, additional margin</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#existing-collateral-additional-margin"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-42" playOrde